[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186083322 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-543c2585-7af9-533a-a269-b37c45eeb579"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-543c2585-7af9-533a-a269-b37c45eeb579" :question/id #uuid "543c2585-7af9-533a-a269-b37c45eeb579" :question/math-academy-id "q-9787" :question/problem "The owner of a restaurant noted that $145$ vegetarian customers visited his restaurant during a particular week. On a particular day of the same week, he noted that $x=15$ vegetarian customers visited the restaurant, corresponding to a $z$-score of $z=-1.5.$ Find the standard deviation of the number of vegetarian customers per day, giving your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the mean number of vegetarian customers for each day:\n\n$$\n\\overset{¯}{x}=\\frac{145}{7}=20.71\n$$\n\nto $2$ decimal places.\n\nThe $z$-score of an observation $x$ is defined by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{\\sigma }.\n$$\n\nThe $z$-score represents how many standard deviations an observation is above or below the mean of the data set. Rewriting this in terms of $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{z}.\n$$\n\nSo, the standard deviation $\\sigma$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sigma  & =\\frac{x-\\overset{¯}{x}}{z} \\\\  & =\\frac{15-20.71}{-1.5} \\\\  & =3.81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nto $2$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-df0001ec-e44a-52b2-ad04-aa3230b4f04d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-df0001ec-e44a-52b2-ad04-aa3230b4f04d" :answer-field/id #uuid "df0001ec-e44a-52b2-ad04-aa3230b4f04d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3ad868d2-4b59-59e5-af41-cdcaa965a99b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dc6c033b-6092-5094-8efd-03c857a491a2" "answer-d87a2113-3ca9-5e90-9173-5ef22a26472f" "answer-b75010ed-05a2-5fae-94e7